$string['tour:coursebanners:glossary:content'] = '<p>A <strong>source</strong> is a banner rule and editing context. It can come from a course category or from a selected custom field value such as a school, campus, programme or audience.</p><div class="local-course-banner-builder-tour-card"><span class="local-course-banner-builder-tour-kicker">Plugin glossary</span><ul class="local-course-banner-builder-tour-list"><li><strong>Inheritance chain</strong>: the ordered path of matching sources used to build a final banner, for example parent category, child category, then a custom field source.</li><li><strong>Source chain</strong>: sources can inherit from parent sources. Inheritance means lower sources can reuse, add to, or replace visual layers coming from higher rules.</li><li><strong>Layers</strong>: visual objects stored inside a source. Image layers hold pictures, border layers frame the banner, overlay layers add colour/transparency, and title settings control Moodle course or activity text.</li><li><strong>Composition</strong>: cumulative mode stacks enabled layers; random mode chooses one eligible image layer while keeping structural layers such as borders and overlays.</li><li><strong>Override</strong>: a layer can change how it behaves in the chain, for example by appearing above a border, overlay or inherited layers.</li></ul></div>';
